<title>JAPAN: Japan offers 400 bln yen in 3.1 pct 20-yr JGBs.</title>
<headline>Japan offers 400 bln yen in 3.1 pct 20-yr JGBs.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance (MOF) said on Tuesday it was offering 400 billion yen in 3.1 percent 20-year Japanese government bonds (JGBs) through a price-competitive auction.</p>
<p>The auction will close at 0300 GMT and the results will be announced at 0530 GMT.</p>
<p>The issue date will be July 22 and the maturity date will be September 20, 2017.</p>
</text>
